{"id":"1d6484d05365d55f","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-fodor-refinement.md","title":"Fodor's Lemma Refinement","display":"thm-fodor-refinement — Fodor's Lemma Refinement","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-fodor-refinement","aliases":["58-thm-fodor-refinement"],"display":"thm-fodor-refinement — Fodor's Lemma Refinement","depends_on":["[[58-df-fodor]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-fodor-refinement"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-fodor-refinement</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-fodor-refinement — Fodor's Lemma Refinement"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d17fa79941daf650\" href=\"?note=d17fa79941daf650\" title=\"58-df-fodor\">58-df-fodor</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\subseteq\\kappa\">\\(S\\subseteq\\kappa\\)</span> is stationary and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega&lt;\\kappa\">\\(\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\)</span> state that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> is regular uncountable</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}refinement}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\n\\land\\operatorname{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\forall\\beta\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\beta)&lt;\\beta)\\Bigr)\n\\to\\exists\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;\\operatorname{Stationary}(f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}],\\kappa).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}refinement}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\n\\land\\operatorname{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\forall\\beta\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\beta)&lt;\\beta)\\Bigr)\n\\to\\exists\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;\\operatorname{Stationary}(f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}],\\kappa).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A refinement of Fodor's lemma: a regressive function is constant on a stationary set.</li>\n<li>More precisely, there is some <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\">\\(\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\\)</span> such that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}]\">\\(f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}]\\)</span> is stationary in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Regular uncountability is part of the formal antecedent rather than only a prose convention.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-fodor","status":"resolved","id":"d17fa79941daf650","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-fodor]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$S\\subseteq\\kappa$ is stationary and $\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)$ (see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"S\\subseteq\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega<\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor\\text{-}refinement}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega<\\kappa\n\\land\\operatorname{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,S,\\kappa)\n\\land\\forall\\beta\\in S\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(f(\\beta)<\\beta)\\Bigr)\n\\to\\exists\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;\\operatorname{Stationary}(f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}],\\kappa).","display":true},{"tex":"\\alpha<\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"f^{-1}[\\{\\alpha\\}]","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false}],"bytes":1268,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4153","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-fodor-refinement.md|58-thm-fodor-refinement]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["d17fa79941daf650","0fbfc19800246e77","36d7463d215be751"]}